   $q$A square is constructed inside a circle of radius $5$ by drawing two perpendicular diameters and joining their endpoints. What is the side length of the square?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-hexagon-rule"},{"text":"$5\\sqrt{2}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$5\\sqrt{3}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-inscribed-triangle-side"},{"text":"$10$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-diameter-as-side"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$5\sqrt{2}$$q$, $q$Each side joins the ends of two perpendicular radii of length $5$, so by the Pythagorean theorem it is $\sqrt{5^2 + 5^2} = 5\sqrt{2}$. The choice $5$ applies the hexagon fact that the side equals the radius, which does not hold for a square.$q$, 'draft', null)
