   $q$To construct a line perpendicular to line $\ell$ at point $P$ on $\ell$, Carmen draws an arc centered at $P$ that crosses $\ell$ at $A$ and $B$. What should Carmen do next?$q$, $q$[{"text":"open the compass wider than $PA$, draw arcs centered at $A$ and $B$ that cross at $Q$, then draw line $PQ$","is_correct":true},{"text":"draw arcs centered at $A$ and $B$ with width $PA$, then join their crossing point to $P$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"kept-width-equal-to-pa"},{"text":"draw a larger arc centered at $P$, then join its ends to $A$ and $B$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"centered-on-wrong-point"},{"text":"draw segment $\\overline{AB}$ and mark its midpoint","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drew-the-given-line"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$open the compass wider than $PA$, draw arcs centered at $A$ and $B$ that cross at $Q$, then draw line $PQ$$q$, $q$Point $P$ is the midpoint of $\overline{AB}$, so the perpendicular bisector of $\overline{AB}$ is the perpendicular at $P$, and it needs arcs wider than $PA$. Arcs of width exactly $PA$ centered at $A$ and $B$ touch only at $P$ itself, so they give no second point.$q$, 'draft', null)
