   $q$The steps for constructing the perpendicular bisector of $\overline{AB}$ are listed out of order. I: Draw line $PQ$. II: Open the compass to more than half of $AB$. III: Without changing the width, draw an arc centered at $B$ that crosses the first arc at $P$ and $Q$. IV: Draw an arc centered at $A$. Which order is correct?$q$, $q$[{"text":"II, IV, III, I","is_correct":true},{"text":"I, II, IV, III","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drew-line-before-arcs"},{"text":"IV, II, III, I","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"set-width-after-drawing-arc"},{"text":"II, IV, I, III","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drew-line-before-second-arc"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$II, IV, III, I$q$, $q$Set the width first (II), draw the arc from $A$ (IV), then the arc from $B$ that creates $P$ and $Q$ (III), and only then draw line $PQ$ (I). Starting with IV draws an arc before the width is chosen, so it may be too small to meet the second arc.$q$, 'draft', null)
