   $q$A square photo frame has outer side length $x + 3$ inches and a square opening with side length $x - 3$ inches. Which expression gives the area of the frame itself, in square inches?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$12x$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$6x$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-double-middle-term"},{"text":"$2x^2 + 18$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-instead-of-subtracted"},{"text":"$0$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"squared-terms-separately"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$12x$$q$, $q$The frame area is $(x + 3)^2 - (x - 3)^2 = (x^2 + 6x + 9) - (x^2 - 6x + 9) = 12x$. The choice $0$ comes from squaring each term separately so that both squares become $x^2 + 9$.$q$, 'draft', null)
