   $q$Mateo cuts a square with side 2.5 inches from the corner of a square sheet of copper with side 7.5 inches. Using $x^2 - y^2 = (x + y)(x - y)$, what is the area of the copper that remains, in square inches?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$62.5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-instead-of-subtracted"},{"text":"$10$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-difference-factor"},{"text":"$50$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$25$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"squared-the-difference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$50$$q$, $q$The remaining area is $7.5^2 - 2.5^2 = (7.5 + 2.5)(7.5 - 2.5) = 10 \cdot 5 = 50$. The choice $25$ computes $(7.5 - 2.5)^2$, which is not the difference of the two areas.$q$, 'draft', null)
