   $q$Which shows $x^4 + 3x^2 - 4$ factored completely over the integers?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$(x^2 + 4)(x^2 - 1)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stopped-factoring-early"},{"text":"$(x^2 - 4)(x^2 + 1)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"swapped-signs-in-factors"},{"text":"$(x + 2)(x - 2)(x + 1)(x - 1)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"factored-sum-of-squares"},{"text":"$(x^2 + 4)(x + 1)(x - 1)$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$(x^2 + 4)(x + 1)(x - 1)$$q$, $q$With $u = x^2$, $u^2 + 3u - 4 = (u + 4)(u - 1)$, so the expression is $(x^2 + 4)(x^2 - 1) = (x^2 + 4)(x + 1)(x - 1)$. The form $(x^2 - 4)(x^2 + 1)$ swaps the signs and expands to $x^4 - 3x^2 - 4$.$q$, 'draft', null)
