   $q$What are all the real solutions of $x^4 - 13x^2 + 36 = 0$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$x = -4$ or $x = -9$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-in-factors"},{"text":"$x = 4$ or $x = 9$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stopped-at-u-values"},{"text":"$x = 2$ or $x = 3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-negative-roots"},{"text":"$x = \\pm 2$ or $x = \\pm 3$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$x = \pm 2$ or $x = \pm 3$$q$, $q$With $u = x^2$, $u^2 - 13u + 36 = (u - 4)(u - 9) = 0$, so $x^2 = 4$ or $x^2 = 9$, giving $x = \pm 2$ or $x = \pm 3$. The choice $x = 4$ or $x = 9$ stops at the values of $u$ instead of solving $x^2 = u$.$q$, 'draft', null)
