   $q$Which expression is a factor of $x^3 + 125$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$x^2 + 5x + 25$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-middle-sign"},{"text":"$x^2 - 5x + 25$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$x^2 - 10x + 25$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"doubled-middle-term"},{"text":"$x - 5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-difference-of-cubes"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$x^2 - 5x + 25$$q$, $q$By the sum of cubes, $x^3 + 125 = (x + 5)(x^2 - 5x + 25)$, so $x^2 - 5x + 25$ is a factor. The trinomial $x^2 + 5x + 25$ belongs to $x^3 - 125$ instead.$q$, 'draft', null)
