   $q$Which is the factored form of $x^2 + 10x + 25 - y^2$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$(x + 5 - y)^2$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrote-perfect-square"},{"text":"$(x + y + 5)(x - y - 5)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"grouped-wrong-terms"},{"text":"$(x + 5 + y^2)(x + 5 - y^2)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-square-root"},{"text":"$(x + 5 + y)(x + 5 - y)$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$(x + 5 + y)(x + 5 - y)$$q$, $q$The first three terms form $(x + 5)^2$, so the expression is $(x + 5)^2 - y^2 = (x + 5 + y)(x + 5 - y)$. The form $(x + y + 5)(x - y - 5)$ equals $x^2 - (y + 5)^2$, which groups the 25 with $y^2$ instead of with $x^2 + 10x$.$q$, 'draft', null)
